  "sourceFinding": "Attempt-20 fixed mesh_particle_radius at 3.0 and found simulation particle_radius 1.6 to have the lowest seven-frame temporal drift at 6.497 percent, still above the frozen 5 percent threshold, while reconstructed volume remained about 31 percent below the frozen source. Blender documents simulation particle_radius for leak or gain correction separately from mesh_particle_radius for reconstructed surface size. This matrix holds the former at 1.6 and varies only the latter.",
  "stopRule": "Stop on process, identity, topology, cache-roster, persistence or resource failure. Every cell must retain exactly config, data and mesh files for frames 1 through 7 and no other Mantaflow cache files. A nested negative shell may subtract from one enclosing positive water surface; more than one positive component, non-nesting, excessive centroid separation, non-manifold geometry, render media, network or engine writes fail closed.",
  "claimCeiling": "Four seven-frame zero-render static controls varying only mesh reconstruction radius with simulation particle radius fixed at 1.6. Even a passing reconstructed-volume candidate still requires a final-resolution static confirmation before slow-tip, impact, lighting or finished-film quality.",
